  "findings": [
    "<b>The matmuls cost about the same</b> in all three (0.8\u20131.0 s of int8 and bf16 matmuls a step); the steps differ in the work around them.",
    "<b>Elementwise ops and copies:</b> 0.38 s for ZenTrainer, 0.88 for AI Toolkit, 1.10 for Fizgig. ComfyUI's comfy-kitchen kernels fuse the quantise and dequantise around each int8 matmul that the others run as separate steps.",
    "<b>Attention:</b> 0.27 s on PyTorch's flash kernel (ZenTrainer), 0.38 on cuDNN (AI Toolkit). Fizgig's padded, masked captions put it on the slower memory-efficient kernel: 1.01 s.",
    "<b>With bf16 matmuls</b> ZenTrainer and AI Toolkit spend the same on matmuls (1.54 and 1.56 s); the gap is again elementwise ops, copies and attention.",
    "<b>Idle:</b> 16 ms a step for ZenTrainer since it reads the GPU once a step (a8c8a6e; 85 ms before)."
  ],
